derivative should be *positive*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t}=kh.\n$$" 13194139534839 true] [17592186313723 1017 #edb/ref 17592186313724 13194139534839 true] [17592186313723 1089 "q-119053" 13194139534839 true] [17592186313723 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534839 true] [17592186313723 1100 "Lucy reads $6$ pages of her new book each day. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the number of pages $P(t)$ Lucy has left to read? Assume that the time $t$ is measured in days." 13194139534839 true] [17592186313723 1113 #uuid "ac92dfbf-ccb9-575c-9ce8-ae4ff8a7a4a6" 13194139534839 true] [17592186313723 1145 "If the number of pages Lucy has left to read is $P$, then the rate of change of the number of the pages is $\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t},$ where $t$ is the time in days.\n\nSince Lucy reads $6$ pages every day, the rate of change of the number of pages she has left is given by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=-6.\n$$\n\nThe right-hand side is negative because the number of pages Lucy has left to read is *decreasing*." 13194139534839 true] [17592186313724 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313725 13194139534839 true] [17592186313724 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313726 13194139534839 true] [17592186313724 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313727 13194139534839 true] [17592186313724 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313728 13194139534839 true] [17592186313724 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313729 13194139534839 true] [17592186313724 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534839 true] [17592186313724 1041 "selection" 13194139534839 true] [17592186313724 1104 #edb/ref 17592186313725 13194139534839 true] [17592186313724 1110 #uuid "5108b9bd-46b0-53ff-a9c8-fbd4081c54ad" 13194139534839 true] [17592186313725 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=-6" 13194139534839 true] [17592186313725 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534839 true] [17592186313725 1111 #uuid "ce12ebed-a77d-55f7-90f8-22c5b9dfbf8b" 13194139534