 told that $\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *number of sales squared.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}∝{S}^{2}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the number of sales *increases* with time, our derivative should be *positive*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=k{S}^{2}.\n$$" 13194139534839 true] [17592186313731 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313732 13194139534839 true] [17592186313731 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313733 13194139534839 true] [17592186313731 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313734 13194139534839 true] [17592186313731 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313735 13194139534839 true] [17592186313731 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313736 13194139534839 true] [17592186313731 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534839 true] [17592186313731 1041 "selection" 13194139534839 true] [17592186313731 1104 #edb/ref 17592186313732 13194139534839 true] [17592186313731 1110 #uuid "18d74731-e3b8-56d6-ac10-f73636d8a859" 13194139534839 true] [17592186313732 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=k{S}^{2},\\,\\,k>0" 13194139534839 true] [17592186313732 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534839 true] [17592186313732 1111 #uuid "cd86361b-c2b2-57c1-8939-9d91a4174c60" 13194139534839 true] [17592186313733 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=-k\\sqrt{S},\\,\\,k>0" 13194139534839 true] [17592186313733 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534839 true] [17592186313733 1111 #uuid "58a97aba-52e7-5dc6-9464-3f0c8f478328" 13194139534839 true] [17592186313734 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=k\\sqrt{S},\\,\\,k>0" 13194139534839 true] [17592186313734 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534839 true] [17592186313734 1111 #uuid "8028e7e8-3b3b-504d-ba91-f836d9cb7c39" 13194139534839 true] [17592186313735 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=-k{S}^{2},\\,\\,k>0" 13194139534839 true] [1759218