$ cubic meters of water every hour. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the volume of water $V(t)$ remaining in the reservoir? Assume that the time $t$ is measured in hours.\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=$  \n{{field-1}}" 13194139534839 true] [17592186313744 1113 #uuid "952f2d49-202a-52d4-9191-44f2632fec2b" 13194139534839 true] [17592186313744 1145 "If the volume of water remaining is $V,$ then the rate of change of the volume is $\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t},$ where $t$ is the time in hours.\n\nSince $14$ cubic meters of water are released each hour, the rate of change of the volume is given by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=-14.\n$$\n\nThe right-hand side is negative because the volume of water is *decreasing*." 13194139534839 true] [17592186313745 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313746 13194139534839 true] [17592186313745 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534839 true] [17592186313745 1041 "field-1" 13194139534839 true] [17592186313745 1104 #edb/ref 17592186313746 13194139534839 true] [17592186313745 1110 #uuid "fa6a76ed-6418-5cda-8e27-b1d632041b70" 13194139534839 true] [17592186313746 1034 "-14" 13194139534839 true] [17592186313746 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534839 true] [17592186313746 1111 #uuid "d3631dab-9cc0-588c-b563-72fe8cee6bab" 13194139534839 true] [17592186313747 1017 #edb/ref 17592186313748 13194139534839 true] [17592186313747 1089 "q-38308" 13194139534839 true] [17592186313747 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534839 true] [17592186313747 1100 "During the winter months, the energy consumption of an average household increases by $1\\,\\text{kWh}$ every week. What differential equation describes the rate of change of energy consumption $E(t)$ (measured in $\\text{kWh}$) of an average household during these months? Assume that the time $t$ is measured in weeks." 13194139534839 true] [17592186313747 1113 #uuid "ee85b646-b59f-5b4a-a6c1-462d95d72046" 13194139534839 true] [17592186313747 1145 "If the energy consumption of an average household is $E\\,\\text{kWh},$ then the rate of change of the energy consumption is $\\frac{\\text{d}E}{\\text{d}t},$ where $t$ is the time in weeks.\n\nSince an additional $1\\,\\text{kWh}$ is consumed every week, the rate of change of the energy consumption is given by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}E}{\\text{d}t}=1.\n$$" 13194139534839 true] [17592186313748 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313749 13194139534839 true] [17592186313748 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313750 13194139534839 true] [17592186313748 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313751 13194139534839 true] [17592186313748 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313752 13194139534839 true] [17592186313748 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313753 13194139534839 true] [17592186313748 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534839 true] [17592186313748 1041 "selection" 13194139534839 true] [17592186313748 1104 #edb/ref 17592186313752 13194139534839 true] [17592186313748 1110 #uuid "87b0ec2c-eb5d-57fd-b5c4-3aebc8c485d4" 13194139534839 true] [17592186313749 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}E}{\\text{d}t}=k,\\,k>0" 13194139534839 true] [17592186313749 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534839 true] [17592186313749 1111 #uuid "692c0428-f099-54bd-9fb1-f2212760fd68" 13194139534839 true] [17592186313750 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}E}{\\text{d}t}=-k,\\,k>0" 13194139534839 true] [17592186313750 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534839 true] [17592186313750 1111 #uuid "ab933d8b-61e5-5b1e-94ab-c3bee5382d22" 13194139534839 true] [17592186313751 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}E}{\\text{d}t}=-1" 13194139534839 true] [17592186313751 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534839 true] [17592186313751 1111 #uuid "601964eb-2d0f-57a4-8aa5-bf28e86a3e72" 13194139534839 true] [17592186313752 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}E}{\\text{d}t}=1" 13194139534839 true] [17592186313752 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534839 true] [17592186313752 1111 #uuid "525a94c7-b1bf-5165-8f37-6ebb93344c1c" 13194139534839 true] [17592186313753 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}E}{\\text{d}t